    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0312" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg262"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 17.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmitted to my Government a copy of
                    your note of May 25 last in relation to the revised regulations for preventing
                    collisions at sea, and I have the honor to inform you that I have been
                    instructed by the Earl of Kimberley to state to you with reference to the
                    concluding paragraph of the letter from Mr. Wike, inclosed in your note, that no
                    alteration will be made for the present in the regulations relating to fishing
                    vessels’ lights. The only regulations repealed by the forthcoming British Order
                    in Council will be those contained in Articles i to ix and xi to xxvii,
                    inclusive, of the schedule to the Order in Council of August 11, 1884.</p>
                <p>The date of the new Order in Council can not at present be fixed, as the
                    principal maritime powers have not yet signified their acceptance of the
                    regulations.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
